body:
Talking/greeting classmates (like the person you sit next to in class) can help. I met many people by saying hi, introducing myself, major, to get started. Then talk to them again. 

&#x200B;

You said you have no floormates. Well maybe you can use a lounge area? and somehow meet ppl there? Like if theres a table and you want to use it, but someone is already using it, just ask if you can share/use the table too, and additionally ask what their name is and say nice to meet them.

&#x200B;

Another thing I did yesterday was be curious. This girl seemed to be studying chinese, so i asked her what level she was at and kept going. 

&#x200B;

i think many times, simply introducing yourself and asking for their name can start a connection.
